<p:sld xmlns:a="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/drawingml/2006/main" xmlns:r="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/officeDocument/2006/relationships" xmlns:p="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/presentationml/2006/main"><p:cSld><p:spTree><p:nvGrpSpPr><p:cNvPr id="1" name=""/><p:cNvGrpSpPr/><p:nvPr/></p:nvGrpSpPr><p:grpSpPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="0" y="0"/><a:ext cx="0" cy="0"/><a:chOff x="0" y="0"/><a:chExt cx="0" cy="0"/></a:xfrm></p:grpSpPr><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="2" name="Title 1"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph type="title"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="990600" y="228600"/><a:ext cx="7161213" cy="814388"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>The Why of the</a:t></a:r><a:br><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/></a:br><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>Cable Effects Study</a:t></a:r><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp><p:sp><p:nvSpPr><p:cNvPr id="3" name="Content Placeholder 2"/><p:cNvSpPr><a:spLocks noGrp="1"/></p:cNvSpPr><p:nvPr><p:ph idx="1"/></p:nvPr></p:nvSpPr><p:spPr><a:xfrm><a:off x="228600" y="1239838"/><a:ext cx="8763000" cy="5183187"/></a:xfrm></p:spPr><p:txBody><a:bodyPr/><a:lstStyle/><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t> Cable harnesses are a large part of spacecraft mass and generally considered a non-structural component at low frequencies. </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>A survey showed that the cable-to-structure mass ratio for DoD and commercial spacecraft can approach 25%.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>Cables are not modeled in detail because no one cared about the “mid frequency” range until a need for better large precision structure models was identified.  </a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" sz="2000" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>Mission performance is driven by on-orbit dynamics: better models are required.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>The program was directed to finding a solution to an Air Force need, not to develop an understanding of the fundamental mechanics of cable behavior.</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr lvl="1"/><a:r><a:rPr lang="en-US" dirty="0" smtClean="0"/><a:t>Applied research</a:t></a:r></a:p><a:p><a:pPr><a:buNone/></a:pPr><a:endParaRPr lang="en-US" dirty="0"/></a:p></p:txBody></p:sp></p:spTree></p:cSld><p:clrMapOvr><a:masterClrMapping/></p:clrMapOvr><p:timing><p:tnLst><p:par><p:cTn id="1" dur="indefinite" restart="never" nodeType="tmRoot"/></p:par></p:tnLst></p:timing></p:sld>